  <para id="para-00011"> <emphasis> Reflections </emphasis></para>
  
>>>>>>> parent of b77700716 (removing hr tags and extra spaces around emphasis)
  <para id="para-00012">Given a function \(f(x)\), a new function \(g(x)=-f(x)\) is a <emphasis>vertical reflection</emphasis> of the function \(f(x)\), sometimes called a reflection about (or over, or through) the \(x\)-axis.</para>
  <para id="para-00013">Given a function \(f(x)\), a new function \(g(x)=f(-x)\) is a <emphasis>horizontal reflection</emphasis> of the function \(f(x)\), sometimes called a reflection about the \(y\)-axis.</para>
      </note>
      <section>
        <title><emphasis>Example</emphasis></title>
        <para id="para-00015">Name the transformations from \(f(x)\) to form \(g(x)=-f(x+4)-8\).</para>
        <para id="para-00016">Horizontal Shift Left 4</para>
        <para id="para-00017">Vertical Shift Down 8</para>
        <para id="para-00018">Reflection? Yes, over the \(x\)-axis.</para>
      </section>
      <note class="try">
        <title>Try It: Transforming Functions</title>
<example id="exam-00001">
          <exercise>
            <problem id="prob-00001">
              <para id="para-00019">Name the transformations from \(f(x)\) to form \(g(x)=-f(x+3)-2\).</para>
              <para id="para-00020">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
            </problem>
            <solution id="sol-00001">
              <para id="para-00021">Here are the transformations made from \(f(x)\) to \(g(x)\):</para>
              <para id="para-00022">Horizontal Shift Left 3</para>
              <para id="para-00023">Vertical Shift Down 2</para>
              <para id="para-00024">Reflection? Yes, over the \(x\)-axis.</para>
            </solution>
          </exercise>
        </example>
      </note>
    </section>
    <section class="check-understanding" id="sect-00002">
      <title>Check Your Understanding</title>
      <exercise id="_96fd3cc6-54f5-4fba-9dd3-31d011575eb9" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00025">Name all of the transformations from \(f(x)\) to form \(g(x)=-f(x+5)-1\).</para>
          <para id="para-00026">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00027">Left 1, Up 5, Reflect over the \(x\)-axis</para>
          <para id="para-00028">Left 5, Down 1, Reflect over the \(x\)-axis</para>
          <para id="para-00029">Left 5, Down 1, Reflect over the \(y\)-axis</para>
          <para id="para-00030">Right 5, Down 1, Reflect over the \(x\)-axis</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
          <para id="para-00031">Correct! Check yourself: The negative in front of the function makes the function reflect over the \(x\)-axis. The constant in \(f(x+5)\) causes a shift left 5, and the constant -1 causes a shift down 1.</para>
          <para id="para-00032">Try again. Take a moment to think about what you learned in the mini-lesson review.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
    </section>
